# Success API

This is a simple API that provides a way to manage users and their properties.

## Maven Shortcuts

### Clean
Clean the `target` directory by removing all compiled files and artifacts:
```
mvn clean
```

### Install
Compile, test, and package the project, and install the package into the local Maven repository:
```
mvn install
```
Or, combine `clean` and `install`:
```
mvn clean install
```

### Build 
Package the project into a JAR/WAR file:
```
mvn package
```

### Run the Application
#### Running with Docker

Start container 
```
docker-compose up
```

Build the Docker image:
```
docker build -t success-api .
```

Run the Docker container:
```
docker run -p 8080:8080 success-api
```

Ensure that Docker is installed and running on your machine before executing these commands.

#### From mvn with host dependacy 
Run the Spring Boot application directly using Maven:
```
mvn spring-boot:run
```
Or, if you have already built the JAR file, you can run it directly using:
```
java -jar target/SUCCESS_WEB_API-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar
```
Make sure to replace `SUCCESS_WEB_API-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar` with the actual name of the generated JAR file.

### Custom CLI
Create system rights if not exist
```
java -jar target/SUCCESS_WEB_API-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar init-rights
```

---

Feel free to adjust the instructions if your API name or version changes!